    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d736">

                <pb facs="1217" n="1203" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1203"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">702.5451/9–1144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the United States Political
                        Adviser, Allied Force Headquarters</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>)<anchor n="48" xml:id="d736-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-11T20:00:00-04:00">September 11,
                            1944—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>124. ReDeptel 96, September 1, 8 p.m.<anchor n="49" xml:id="d736-f2"/> German
                    occupying authorities forced Swiss Consulates at Marseille and Nice to evacuate
                    to Montelimar and Grenoble respectively. Department believes that they should
                    return as facilities and opportunities for protection of United States and
                    British nationals are not so favorable inland as at Marseille and Nice. Please
                    discuss matter with military authorities and inform Department of result in
                    order that this may be taken up with Swiss Government.<anchor n="50"
                        xml:id="d736-f3"/> Department views this step as of considerable importance
                    in view of its probable inability to open offices in southern France for some
                    time to come.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d736-f1" n="48" type="source" xml:id="d736-f1-content">
                <p>Mr. Kirk served concurrently (as Political Adviser to the Supreme Allied
                    Commander, Mediterranean Theater, whose Allied Force Headquarters (AFHQ) was at
                    Caserta, and as American member of the Advisory Council for Italy, with a staff
                    at Caserta and a staff at Rome.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d736-f2" n="49" xml:id="d736-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d736-f3" n="50" xml:id="d736-f3-content">
                <p>The Minister in Switzerland was advised in telegram 3252, September 21, noon, to
                    inform the Swiss Foreign Office that military authorities in southern France
                    were under instructions to facilitate; return of Swiss Consuls to Marseille and
                    Nice (702.5451/9–2144).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
